<article class="env-lemma" id="0GLD">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0GLD">Lemma <span data-tag="0GLD">63.11.6</span>.</a> Let $f : X \to Y$ be a separated finite type morphism of quasi-separated and quasi-compact schemes. Let $\Lambda $ be a torsion ring. For every $K \in D(Y_{\acute{e}tale}, \Lambda )$ and $L \in D(X_{\acute{e}tale}, \Lambda )$ the map (<a href="/tag/0GLB" data-tag="0GLB">63.11.4.1</a>) induces an isomorphism </p>
  <div class="equation">
  \[  R\mathop{\mathrm{Hom}}\nolimits _ X(L, Rf^!K) \longrightarrow R\mathop{\mathrm{Hom}}\nolimits _ Y(Rf_!L, K)  \]
</div>
  <p> of global derived homs. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      By the construction in Cohomology on Sites, Section <a href="/tag/0B6E" data-tag="0B6E">21.36</a> we have 
    <p>
      <div class="equation">
  \[  R\mathop{\mathrm{Hom}}\nolimits _ X(L, Rf^!K) = R\Gamma (X, R\mathop{\mathcal{H}\! \mathit{om}}\nolimits _\Lambda (L, Rf^!K)) = R\Gamma (Y, Rf_*R\mathop{\mathcal{H}\! \mathit{om}}\nolimits _\Lambda (L, Rf^!K))  \]
</div>
    <p>
       (the second equality by Leray) and 
    <p>
      <div class="equation">
  \[  R\mathop{\mathrm{Hom}}\nolimits _ Y(Rf_!L, K) = R\Gamma (Y, R\mathop{\mathcal{H}\! \mathit{om}}\nolimits _\Lambda (Rf_!L, K))  \]
</div>
    <p>
       Thus the lemma is a consequence of Lemma <a href="/tag/0GLC" data-tag="0GLC">63.11.5</a>. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>